---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/config';
---
<Layout lang="en" title="About Stille" description="Stille is an independent open-source peer-to-peer messenger for Android. Learn about its architecture, encryption and limits." canonical="/en/about/">
<Header />
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="document-page wrap">
  <PageIntro label="About" title="Stille — quiet by design" description="An independent open-source messenger where attention stays on the conversation, not the decoration around it." />
  <section class="document-grid about-section" aria-labelledby="architecture-heading"><div><h2 id="architecture-heading">The app and the core</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>The Android client is built on stille-messenger-core. The core handles connections and cryptography; the app handles the interface, profile, contacts and conversations.</p><p>Stille uses peer-to-peer connections over an available route. Local discovery, direct connections or a self-hosted relay may be possible depending on the network.</p><div class="source-links"><a href={site.android} rel="noreferrer">Android client ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/puxxalwl/stille-messenger-core" rel="noreferrer">Messaging core ↗</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="document-grid about-section" aria-labelledby="security-heading"><div><h2 id="security-heading">Encryption and trust</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>The project documents end-to-end post-quantum encryption; the core manages keys and cryptography. The source code is available for inspection.</p><p>Open source does not mean an independent security audit has been completed. We do not promise absolute anonymity: connection properties depend on the route and configuration.</p></div></section>
  <section class="document-grid about-section" aria-labelledby="license-heading"><div><h2 id="license-heading">Publisher and license</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Stille Messenger Website is published by <strong>Puxxalwl and EryynIT</strong> and licensed under <a href="https://github.com/Puxxalwl/stille-messenger-website/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noreferrer">AGPL-3.0-or-later ↗</a>. Original Android and core projects retain their respective notices and licenses.</p><p>Questions, feedback and project contact: <a href="https://t.me/puxalwl" rel="noreferrer">Puxxalwl @puxalwl ↗</a> and <a href="https://t.me/eprintln" rel="noreferrer">EryyynIT @eprintln ↗</a>.</p></div></section>
  <section class="document-grid about-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading"><div><h2 id="privacy-heading">This website</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>There is no analytics, advertising or external font loading. The browser stores only your selected theme.</p><p>Invite codes are processed locally. The site does not send them to a QR service or store them, but the URL remains visible to the host and in browser history.</p></div></section>
  <section class="project-contact"><h2>Contribute</h2><p>Found a bug or want to suggest an improvement? Start with the repository or contact the maintainer.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${site.android}/issues`} rel="noreferrer">Open a GitHub issue ↗</a> · <a class="text-link" href="https://t.me/puxalwl" rel="noreferrer">Puxxalwl on Telegram ↗</a> · <a class="text-link" href="https://t.me/eprintln" rel="noreferrer">EryynIT on Telegram ↗</a></section>
</main><Footer />
</Layout>
